# Staff authentication setup:
# 1. npm run db:deploy
# 2. npm run staff:create -- --email admin@example.com --name "Administrator" --role super
#    Enter a new 12-128 character password at the hidden prompts.
#    This is an operator-only CLI; no public registration or default credentials exist.
#
# JWTs use RS256 and expire after one hour. The private/public key pair is generated
# on first login and persisted in StaffSigningKey, shared across restarts/replicas.
# No STAFF_API_KEY or JWT-secret environment variable is required.
# Restrict database access and protect backups: the signing private key is sensitive.
# Deleting the StaffSigningKey row invalidates all issued JWTs; next login makes a new key.
# Login response accessToken is sent in Authorization, never x-admin-role/x-staff-key.
# Legacy identity headers remain CORS-allowed for compatibility, but confer no staff access.
# Do not persist bearer tokens in URLs, logs, source code or localStorage.
#
# API consumers must add a login screen and derive visible permissions from /auth/me.
# Handle 401 by clearing the session and returning to sign-in; 403 means insufficient role.
# Logout revokes ALL tokens for that account. Role/password/disabled changes revoke tokens.
# /auth/password also revokes all tokens; sign in again with the new password.
#
# Creator routes/uploads now require a staff JWT linked to the artist:
# npm run staff:create -- --email artist@example.com --name "Artist" --role creator --creator-id meera
# Artist registration alone does not grant a staff account. x-creator-id is not trusted
# on protected creator endpoints. Fulfilment requires operations or super.
#
# Run npm run test:auth for isolated tests (database calls mocked).
# npm run smoke MUTATES the configured DB and storage; run only on a disposable test DB.
# Its temporary staff fixtures are removed after the run; ordinary business fixtures remain.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@accessToken = REPLACE_WITH_LOGIN_RESPONSE_TOKEN

### Sign in (role is loaded from the database, not accepted in the request).
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_PASSWORD"
}

### Current account, with no password hash.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Admin identity and permitted desks.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Only super administrators can create accounts.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "moderator@example.com",
  "name": "Moderator",
  "password": "REPLACE_WITH_A_NEW_PASSWORD",
  "role": "moderator"
}

### List staff (super only).
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Change another account's role/disabled state/password (super only).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auth/staff/REPLACE_WITH_STAFF_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "disabled": true
}

### Change own password.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_PASSWORD",
  "newPassword": "REPLACE_WITH_A_NEW_PASSWORD"
}

### Revoke all sessions for this account.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
